course: dictionary
lesson: 4619
title: Words for high places
level: primary-4
stars: 1
explain: Highland is a word for land that is high up, with hills and mountains. Lowland is the opposite: flat, low ground. Geography books use these words to describe the shape of the land.
explain: The Highlands are a name for a real place: the mountainous north and west part of Scotland. Capital H and a name tell you it is a place. Here is a sentence from a science book: «The Scottish Highlands and the Appalachian Mountains of North America are parts of the same ancient mountain chain.» Ancient means very old, so this mountain chain is very old.
explain: Highland can also be an adjective, a describing word, as in Highland cattle or Highland dancing. Look at the word next to it: if it describes a thing, it is an adjective. Check with the context: which word tells you what kind of thing it is?
fact: A highland is land that is high up, with hills and mountains.
fact: Highlands are often colder, wetter and less crowded than lowlands.
fact: The Highlands are the mountainous north and west part of Scotland.
fact: Highland games include tossing the caber, and Highland cattle and bagpipes are famous Scottish things.
fact: Many countries have highlands, such as the Ethiopian Highlands.
exercise: Highlands are areas of high ground. What is the opposite of highlands in geography? | Deserts | Islands | Oceans | *Lowlands
exercise: «The Scottish Highlands and the Appalachian Mountains of North America are parts of the same ancient mountain chain.» What does ancient mean here? | Very wet | Very new | *Very old | Very high
exercise: Which phrase uses highland as an adjective, describing a thing? | We walked in the highlands | The highlands are cold | *Highland cattle | Highlands is a place
test: Which is the best meaning of «the Highlands» as a name? | A big city in England | A river in Wales | *The mountainous north and west part of Scotland | A type of Scottish bagpipe
test: In «formed over 400 million years ago», what does formed mean? | Painted in bright colours | Lost or hidden | *Made or created over a long time | Sung loudly
exam: Many countries have highlands. Which country has the Ethiopian Highlands? | Australia | Scotland | *Ethiopia | Canada
